WEBVTT

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:48.250
The EX-1 is now being
repaired at the Funeral base...

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.190
...using its self-repair features.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.250
The report suggests

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:57.500
that at this rate, it should be ready
for action again within 178 hours.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.310
Within a week, eh?

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:04.020
Should we consider that fast or slow?

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.970
I believe it depends on the alien.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.110
Depends on the alien, eh?

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.780
The alien surprised us
the way it went after Funeral.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.770
We should have anticipated that.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:26.040
Our strategy for interception
was straight out of the book -

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:31.410
Manual 12, ream 3-1 from
the Ministry of Defense's A report.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.930
At each stage, accuracy was near
perfectly in line with projections.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.760
This became the best record
for any strategy we've ever had.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:48.230
This is a chart of our counterattack
and its distribution and damage.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.570
I understand that most of our missiles hit.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.520
But what I don't get is why
that didn't destroy the alien.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:59.870
As I explained, if this
had been a normal alien...

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:06.380
...there's at least a 78% chance
our tactics would have finished it.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:12.040
But we failed because it had more
capabilities than we thought.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:17.890
I don't think it was a problem
with our overall interception.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:21.390
That's what's normally called an excuse.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.690
Speaking of that...

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:28.940
Wasn't the nuclear warhead
on the EX-1 actually a dummy?

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.480
You said you will take responsibility,

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.650
but it was just words with no action.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:41.210
About the warhead, the EX-1
may have greater applications...

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.960
What are you talking about?

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.000
We're the ones that requested
the safety net for emergencies.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.670
If you have any doubt
about what could happen...

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.000
Stop it!

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.090
We're not here to argue
if the warhead was real or not.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:02.090
The reason we're here is to unify
our mind toward defense efforts.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:05.550
Lieutenant.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.190
We're running out of time.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.350
Could you wrap it up, please.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.950
Y-Yes, sir.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:16.580
I'd like to report the need for
improved defense and summarize...

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.540
You can prepare the document
and submit it to me later.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.130
Then let me just quickly give an overview.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.200
These damned things never end.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.970
You may think that this has no meaning,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.270
but it's an important ceremony.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:41.640
You need to be patient.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.140
Ceremony?

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:46.770
To show the politicians and the bureaucrats...

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.470
...that we're working hard to fight off the aliens.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:55.770
And for the press, who are also
after the military's actions, no?

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.250
Any way you slice it, it's a difficult job.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.870
The next report, please.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.840
With animal behavioral science

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:13.630
we've analyzed how the aliens
operate and isolated certain patterns.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.640
If you would please refer to
page 2896 of the reports...

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.980
...section 234, table 568.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.110
There have been many debates

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.860
concerning invasion and the aliens' goals.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.860
For example, using standard
movement vector and filtering,

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:36.160
we get images that can be laid on a map.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:42.670
Clearly, all vectors converge on the same point.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:49.040
We get the same results
each time, no exceptions.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:55.510
It's quite natural to conclude there
is a target guiding their behavior.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:06:05.140
But the data from the last incident
has moved us to rethink that.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.860
What do you mean?

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:11.990
The last alien's action,
directly attacking its enemy

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.450
gives weight to the idea
that there is another purpose

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.540
apart from the mere conquest of our world.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:25.350
This represents a backtracking
from our other hypotheses.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:26.740
Chairman?

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.130
Recognized.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.800
About the comment just presented...

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:36.720
I don't agree we can infer that
the alien intended to engage Funeral.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:39.630
It's too early to conclude that.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:45.600
Isn't it more reasonable to assume
the base was merely in its way...

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:49.600
...and that this was not
part of any master plan?

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.650
When performing a scientific analysis,

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:57.270
we have to look for evidence
that supports our hypotheses.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:01.910
Also, we need to explain the event...

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.240
...from a logical and realistic point of view.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:14.500
So it's not scientific to say they're all
converging at the Pilgrimage Point?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.890
The term "Pilgrimage Point" is one
we decided to use temporarily,

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:21.590
so a more accurate term should...

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:25.510
I don't care what words we use!

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:28.820
What we have to figure out

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:32.530
is the military's response to the invasion.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.950
According to this conversation,

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:40.040
the military believes the aliens'
purpose is invasion and none other.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.570
Is that correct?

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.880
As I've said,

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.280
I don't think we're in
a position to debate that yet.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.630
In other words,

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:55.800
You'll theorize that the alien
intended to destroy Funeral,

00:07:55.890 --> 00:08:00.520
but to assume that all the other
aliens will do the same thing

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.690
when they regroup at the
Pilgrimage Point isn't "scientific."

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:10.990
Until they've reached
the convergence point,

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:15.620
it would be wrong to use
a word like "invasion."

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:19.780
Again, I don't think we should
waste time arguing semantics.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:25.770
Tell us then why this attack refutes
evidence from the other invasions.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.710
Give us your scientific explanation.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.260
Well...

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:35.010
For one thing, we don't have
enough data to draw conclusions...

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:36.080
This is...

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.770
...a simple matter of common sense!

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:45.020
We don't know where they came
from and how they got here,

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.610
but we know the Earth isn't big enough

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:53.610
that they happened to stop by
on their way traveling through space.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.530
It may not have been clear what they wanted,

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:01.660
but now that they've shown up
in such large numbers,

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.150
it's obvious they have a reason!

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:06.040
Everyone is with me so far, right?

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:12.590
But all of them are heading
for one point on the map.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.440
How do you explain that?

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:20.840
Do you know of the military's
Star System Operation?

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:25.440
I think I know what it is in theory.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:27.850
Then that makes this easier.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.690
I haven't had much experience,

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:35.660
but the idea is that it's impossible
to pinpoint a single location

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:40.080
on Earth from outside a solar system,
regardless of technology.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.990
Isn't that right, Professor?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.710
Y-Yes!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:48.250
Even with the highest caliber telescope,

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.050
all we can get is a rough idea
of the planets themselves.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:58.180
So we have to conclude that the aliens,
until they reached Earth,

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:03.300
wouldn't have any information about the Earth.

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:06.300
Which only logically leads to one theory.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:10.530
Obviously, the behavior of the aliens in the past

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:15.070
is to first amass intelligence
and then move to an outpost to...

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.540
That's a self-serving analysis of the situation.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.620
Come again?

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:25.030
The military is trying to play up the threat
and vilify the other side.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:27.990
Are you saying we've
made the whole thing up?

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.800
It’s just frustrating.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.090
We're dealing with an important problem...

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:37.350
...and the military’s just interested
in touting its own importance.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:41.560
Especially with the budget talks
for the next fiscal year coming.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:45.390
The extra funds this new
defense package would mean...

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:46.560
That's crap!

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:50.150
Are you saying we don't
care about global security?

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.770
You politicians...

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:55.320
...don't have any idea how to solve this problem,

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:57.230
so you’re just trying to make us look bad!

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.190
Quiet!

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.920
Quiet!

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.250
This isn't the place for partisan bickering.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.590
Commander Ines!

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:18.260
As our representative from
the front lines, what do you think?

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.740
When they are attacked for no reason,

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:37.060
or cornered by many,
particularly when they are alone,

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:41.410
even the tamest animal
will fight wildly for its life.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.630
I'm sorry.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.990
I was just thinking about that fight
with the alien the other day.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.140
"Alone"?

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.140
When did I start thinking
of them like humans?

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:04.890
Our main purpose is to fight
the aliens on the front lines.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:10.470
I think it is beyond our duty
to question what their purpose is.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:14.820
Even though the fight may be avoidable,

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:18.440
as long as it's our duty,
we must go and fight the aliens.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.460
That's how we look at it.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.500
However, if I might be allowed to say...

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:30.870
No, never mind.

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:34.390
What if we don't interfere
with alien movement...

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:38.590
...but let them go where they want
and find out what they're up to?

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:40.430
You can't be serious!

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:45.190
Who will take the responsibility
when they do the unthinkable?

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:47.890
Responsibility.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.570
Responsibility...

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:56.690
Yes, we might already be guilty
with what we've done so far.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:58.080
More crap!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:02.040
You're saying we're responsible
for defending ourselves?

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.420
Take that back!

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.210
No...

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:13.260
No, I certainly misspoke.

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:16.960
But what I'd like us all to keep in mind...

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.230
...is that however strong our duty
to intercept the aliens is,

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:25.690
we've actually uprooted
a number of people's lives

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:29.070
and harmed civilians in the process.

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:32.700
That naturally makes one
feel emotionally uneasy.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.910
Dr. Takahashi.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:42.910
Eh?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.130
Would you care to tell us

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.250
what you've found out
about the Pilgrimage Point?

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.160
Yes, sir.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:52.800
You know how to
touch nerves, don't you?

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:53.750
Honestly.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:02.090
Well, the reason I was called upon
to take part in this project is...

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.560
We don't need to know
your personal background, sir.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.230
Just proceed to the main point.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.030
Yes, of course.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:13.950
Well, let's turn our attentions
to Pilgrimage Point.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:20.250
We first theorized that there
could be something special

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:25.460
about this point when we noticed
the aliens were heading toward it.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.080
We've heard this a thousand times.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.510
What? Oh, you have?

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:34.260
Well, you see, our team's been
trying to identify the connection

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:38.100
between the point and the aliens
examining all available data.

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:43.230
However, though we've employed
a number of different models...

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:47.690
Well, as seen on page 3382 of the report,

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:51.990
we've analyzed the soil composition,
air, radiation levels,

00:14:51.990 --> 00:15:02.040
weather patterns for the last 200 years,
UFO sightings, everything.

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:08.800
We've yet to find anything that would
account for the level of interest.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.290
Therefore...

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.250
Therefore!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:16.800
...you're saying there's no connection
between the point and the aliens?

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.600
Correct?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.020
Well, in a manner of speaking...

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:24.810
But on the other hand,
we've calculated the likelihood

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:27.680
that the vector overlap could be coincidence,

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:31.280
and the probability is less than
10 to the minus 32 power...

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:35.990
...or for all intents and purposes, zero.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.360
So what are you trying to say, man?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:44.700
That based on evidence, a scientific
answer may be the problem.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:51.340
Then we wondered if the answer
could be found in the past

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:55.220
and researched local folklore.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.250
Folklore?

00:15:56.550 --> 00:16:00.730
The mythological traditions handed
down through the generations.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:04.690
We wondered whether the natives
originally inhabiting the region

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:12.060
might have some legend about
UFOs or similar anecdotes.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.530
And what did you find?

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:17.410
We did find one man who recounted stories.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:21.030
Unfortunately, we learned
that he had passed away.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:27.460
We tracked down the family record
and found a descendant...

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:37.060
...but the man was a punk with no
knowledge of legends or culture.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.810
Young people today are so absorbed...

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.350
So there's no information
about Pilgrimage Point

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:46.820
or what it means to the aliens, correct?

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:49.440
Precisely, sir.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.600
So it's like we said.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:57.580
There's no other reason
for the aliens to be coming here.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:01.580
Stop trying to force your conclusion.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:05.920
If we give the military free reign,
you'll snatch up all the budget...

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:06.960
lf...

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.050
...the purpose of the aliens
has not been invasion...

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:17.340
...all the damage we've done trying
to stop them has been for nothing.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:20.270
If that's the case, it won't just be the military,

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:24.890
but the government as well that
will be subject to public criticism.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.940
We clearly cannot allow that to happen.

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:35.310
I want everyone here to be mindful
of that when expressing your views.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:39.790
The scope of this issue extends
beyond that of a simple turf war.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:44.700
The survival of this body depends
upon this challenge's response.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:51.160
Are you saying it no longer matters
if this is an alien invasion or not?

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:55.340
What matters most is what serves
our ultimate objectives in the end.

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:56.380
Is that not correct?

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.900
In other words, you're saying...

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:08.600
...as far as we're concerned,
it has to be an alien invasion.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:14.410
If we hadn't seen civilian casualties
or damage to the cities,

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:17.870
we might be able to justify any decision.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:22.460
But unfortunately, the time of
innocence passed long ago.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:28.160
In other words, we have no choice.
Even if we have to alter the truth?

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:32.620
Do you seriously believe there is
truth within the context of politics?

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.790
One of the aliens...

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:42.760
...the EX-1 can communicate
telepathically with a human girl.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.650
I've heard about that.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.350
Sounds like something out of a movie.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:54.440
We haven't learned yet how the girl
and the EX-1 communicate.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.200
But the only thing we do know clearly...

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.900
...is that aliens' thought processes...

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:04.360
...are not so completely different from humans'.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.870
What are you trying to say?

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.630
We've been treating the alien arrival

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:14.180
like it were some kind of natural disaster.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:15.330
But...

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:19.930
But if we suppose the aliens have
the same mental capabilities we do...

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:23.400
Don't be ridiculous!

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.940
I thought maybe you had
something important to say.

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.010
Don't feed us romance novels.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:31.030
Whatever you do, you're still a woman.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.580
Commander Ines.

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:58.000
I don't know much about
the Funeral organization...

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:01.590
...but it seems most of
your pilots are very young.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:02.940
Yes, sir.

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:06.560
Most of my troops are in their twenties.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.530
Is that relevant?

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:12.360
No, I just thought so when I looked at you.

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:19.410
Anyway, just forget about today
and go take care of your troops.

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:27.750
Please, return the hard copies.

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:32.250
I'm afraid today's meeting was classified.

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.140
Sure.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:06.000
Like a little skylark, isn't it?

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.740
A pretty, little doll.

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:10.970
When you realize how fragile it is,

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:13.120
you handle it with extra care.

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:17.260
Trouble is, once it's well
enough to go out on its own,

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:20.430
it may never come back.

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:22.190
What are you talking about?

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:23.560
What?

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:26.100
Pretending you don't know again?

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.650
You know what I'm talking about.

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:31.490
The doll that will never return to you...

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.640
That's the alien...

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.860
and the other you in you.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:38.450
And also...

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:46.340
The remains that have flown away
but still live inside your memory.

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:49.260
You've grown up.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.870
You've matured so much.

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:56.840
You're always eating.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:00.980
Humans just exist to eat, digest, and expel.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:04.020
Isn't that right, Takuto Kaneshiro?

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:05.520
Seems like a big waste.

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:07.940
And I suppose it is.

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:13.860
But when you think about it,
that's all that life really is.

00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:18.950
Now that you mention it,
he doesn't eat, does he?

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.580
Why does he exist?

00:22:36.550 --> 00:22:39.220
The death will come belated.

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:43.980
Because the spirits of the dead
are filling Valhalla.

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:48.860
Next time,
Chaos and Confusion.
